WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.880
Speaker 1: Welcome back to the David Pakman show.&nbsp;
I am Ferron Cousins from Ring of Fire sitting in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:11.280
for David Pakman today. Now, if you tuned in&nbsp;
to the program yesterday, you heard producer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:17.760
Pat doing a wonderful job talking about Donald&nbsp;
Trump, going after Mitch McConnell, going after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:23.360
Elaine Chao. And I don't want to beat a dead horse&nbsp;
here, but I do want to take a couple of minutes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:31.360
and talk about that story one more time, because&nbsp;
I do believe that there's more that we need to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:37.120
looking at here. So in case you missed the story&nbsp;
yesterday, Donald Trump over the weekend came out.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:44.000
Let me just read it. This is what he put on&nbsp;
through social. Why do Republican senators allow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:49.680
a broken down hack politician, Mitch McConnell to&nbsp;
openly disparage hardworking Republican candidates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:55.680
for the United States Senate? This is such an&nbsp;
affront to honor and to leadership. He should&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.680 --> 00:01:01.440
spend more time and money helping them get elected&nbsp;
and less time helping his crazy wife and family&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:08.480
get rich on China. So, of course, Elaine Chao&nbsp;
was Donald Trump's transportation secretary.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.800
And yes, there were plenty of, you know,&nbsp;
allegations against her while she was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:18.240
transportation secretary that she was steering&nbsp;
federal money towards her family business. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:25.840
were going to investigate that. But then after she&nbsp;
resigned, after January 6th, the DOJ just said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:33.760
forget it, let bygones be bygones. Right. That's&nbsp;
terrible. And of course, it was Trump's DOJ. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:41.360
that doesn't mean the DOJ couldn't still do that.&nbsp;
Right. I mean, there were credible allegations.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:46.080
There was evidence that suggested that she was&nbsp;
using her position to benefit her family business.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:52.160
Kind of sounds like the thing we ought to be&nbsp;
investigating, right? Isn't that the kind of thing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:59.440
that we want to root out of politics? But all of&nbsp;
that aside. It's the attack on Mitch McConnell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:06.800
himself that really stuck out to me because Trump,&nbsp;
like everybody else in this country, looks at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:12.640
poll numbers. And right now, those poll numbers&nbsp;
show that not only are Democrats most likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:16.800
going to retain control of the Senate, but they're&nbsp;
probably going to pick up a couple of seats, too.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:26.320
They could end up picking up seats in Wisconsin,&nbsp;
Pennsylvania and Ohio, as well as holding on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:31.360
to seats that they previously thought they&nbsp;
may not including in the state of Georgia.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:37.520
So Democrats are sitting pretty. Republicans&nbsp;
are running out of money. You know, thanks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:42.000
to Rick Scott being a horrible manager of the&nbsp;
National Republican Senatorial Campaign Committee,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:47.200
they're running out of money. They're&nbsp;
pulling ads in crucial swing states,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:53.840
including Wisconsin and Pennsylvania that I&nbsp;
just mentioned. And so they need a fall guy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.960 --> 00:03:00.320
They need somebody to blame for the fact that&nbsp;
Republicans in the Senate are doing very bad.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:07.600
Enter Mitch McConnell, right. Donald Trump, as we&nbsp;
all know, has been going after Mitch McConnell for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:14.720
months and months and months, just absolutely&nbsp;
trashing the guy earlier this year and last year,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:21.440
of course, trying to get people to run for Senate&nbsp;
by pledging that they will not vote for Mitch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:26.480
McConnell to be in a leadership position again.&nbsp;
He only got two people, by the way, to sign on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:33.360
to that whole deal. But this is something Trump&nbsp;
has been laying the groundwork for for a year,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:42.880
replacing Mitch McConnell. So what he is doing&nbsp;
right now has less to do with McConnell's wife,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:48.320
has nothing to do with the investigations&nbsp;
that should be taking place. He is setting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:54.400
McConnell up to take the fall for the fact&nbsp;
that Republicans put forth some bad candidates.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.160 --> 00:04:02.800
And the irony here, of course, is that these&nbsp;
candidates that are likely going to lose these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:08.720
are all Trump backed candidates. Ron Johnson in&nbsp;
Wisconsin, the latest poll numbers show him doing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:15.280
terribly right now. Well, he's also implicated&nbsp;
in the fake elector scheme. But don't worry.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:20.960
He said this week he came out. He's like, I was&nbsp;
only involved in it for, quote, seconds. Okay.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:27.840
Well, you were still involved by your own&nbsp;
admission now. So good luck with that in court.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:33.200
Then you have, of course, Dr. Oz in&nbsp;
Pennsylvania. We all know how that's going.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:39.040
Herschel Walker in Georgia, terrible campaign&nbsp;
with a terrible candidate, J.D. Vance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:44.000
up in Ohio, who Trump thought was going to&nbsp;
be the golden boy. Can't even beat Tim Ryan.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:52.000
So all of Trump's people are failing. And&nbsp;
Mitch McConnell has been coming out recently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:57.840
blaming Trump without having to name him for&nbsp;
basically saddling the Republican Party with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:02.800
these horrible candidates. So Trump is&nbsp;
trying to flip the script. Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:06.960
blame it all on McConnell because&nbsp;
his leadership is just terrible.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:12.480
So he can finally oust the man that he&nbsp;
has had this personal vendetta against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:21.120
for over a year. Probably not going to work.&nbsp;
Probably wouldn't work out well for Republicans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:26.880
anyway, even if that happened. Because as horrible&nbsp;
of a human being as I believe that Mitch McConnell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:32.480
is. He is good at what he does. Now, what&nbsp;
he does is terrible, don't get me wrong.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:38.480
But that guy knows how to play the game. That&nbsp;
guy knows how to manipulate people. He knows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:44.560
how to be sneaky, conniving, backstabbing, all of&nbsp;
that. That's how he's gotten so far ahead in life.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:50.240
So if you remove that guy from the top of your&nbsp;
party, you're going to suffer. Democrats are going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:57.440
to do so much better. So I guess what I'm saying&nbsp;
is keep up the crusade, Donald, because I would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.440 --> 00:06:02.400
love nothing more than to see Mitch McConnell&nbsp;
ousted from leadership, because that's going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:08.000
create a massive void within the Republican Party&nbsp;
that I don't think any of you know how to fill.

